[{:db/id "q-330948/field-1/826b1f2e52ed50749521e5caca4473ba777777c2a16aae6d16bc7a5751283043" :answer/id #uuid "c1a94faa-ef95-51eb-b9b6-a36d71297684" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{18}{s^3}+\\frac{24}{s^2}+\\frac{16}{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-330948/field-1/4dccbf089fe7828513c7401b16662d905aef6079c03c4ff157e056c5e011da9d" :answer/id #uuid "5a2057fd-fafc-5925-b237-102e4ef70503" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{s^3}+\\frac{24}{s^2}+\\frac{16}{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-330948/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "4673e41b-2429-50a1-b9b4-22206955e8a4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-330948/field-1/826b1f2e52ed50749521e5caca4473ba777777c2a16aae6d16bc7a5751283043" :answer-field/choices ["q-330948/field-1/826b1f2e52ed50749521e5caca4473ba777777c2a16aae6d16bc7a5751283043" "q-330948/field-1/4dccbf089fe7828513c7401b16662d905aef6079c03c4ff157e056c5e011da9d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-330948" :question/id #uuid "3c294091-0460-52e0-836a-793055353031" :question/math-academy-id "q-330948" :question/problem "Given that $L{{t}^{n}}=\\frac{n!}{{s}^{n+1}},$ find the Laplace transform of $f(t)=(3t+4)^{2}$ for $s>0.$\n\n$L{f(t)}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The linearity property of the Laplace transform states that for functions $f(t)$ and $g(t),$ we have\n\n$$\nL{\\alpha f(t)+\\beta g(t)}=\\alpha \\cdot L{f(t)}+\\beta \\cdot L{g(t)}\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants.\n\nFirst, we expand:\n\n$$\nf(t)=(3t+4)^{2}=9{t}^{2}+24t+16\n$$\n\nTaking the Laplace transform and applying the linearity properties, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{f(t)} & =L{9{t}^{2}+24t+16} \\\\  & =L{9{t}^{2}}+L{24t}+L{16} \\\\  & =9L{{t}^{2}}+24L{t}+16L{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that $L{{t}^{n}}=\\frac{n!}{{s}^{n+1}}.$ Therefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{t}^{2}} & =\\frac{2}{{s}^{3}},\\,s>0 \\\\ L{t} & =\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}},\\,s>0 \\\\ L{1} & =\\frac{1}{s},\\,s>0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Laplace transform of $f(t)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{f(t)} & =9L{{t}^{2}}+24L{t}+16L{1} \\\\  & =9\\cdot \\frac{2}{{s}^{3}}+24\\cdot \\frac{1}{{s}^{2}}+16\\cdot \\frac{1}{s} \\\\  & =\\frac{18}{{s}^{3}}+\\frac{24}{{s}^{2}}+\\frac{16}{s} \\\\  & =\\frac{18+24s+16{s}^{2}}{{s}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(8{s}^{2}+12s+9)}{{s}^{3}},\\,s>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-330948/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cb99e6f5-005f-543f-b6c9-a0dc1c304d99"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-330948"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-332674/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "e446462f-5423-5004-b0c3-12566bdb6eb9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332674/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "f4c63880-b7b2-5eaf-8275-bd7a4773abc0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332674/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "28d2b936-e050-57b9-8204-c393a10ba8d3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332674/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "1efef38f-fe16-5ef1-957f-39dc877af1cf" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332674/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "c6818764-ab64-502e-9553-05d0e9a4726e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332674/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "52658998-d645-56f6-b5df-343b402efc53" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-332674/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer-field/choices ["q-332674/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-332674/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-332674/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-332674/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-332674/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-332674" :question/id #uuid "08f4acd9-0162-5e07-b55e-d0e4a1671202" :question/math-academy-id "q-332674" :question/problem "Let $f(t)$ be a piecewise function defined on $[0,\\infty )$ with exponential order $a,$ and consider its Laplace transform \n\n$$\nF(s)=L{f(t)},\\,s>a.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- If $f(t)$ contains a discontinuity for some value of $t>0,$ we have $F(s)=0$ for all $s>a.$\n- $F(s)$ is infinitely differentiable on $s>a.$\n- The Laplace transform converts a non-smooth $f(t)$ into a smooth function of $s.$" :question/worked-solution "If a function $f(t)$ is piecewise continuous on $[0,\\infty )$ and has exponential order $a,$ then its Laplace transform\n\n$$\nF(s)=L{f(t)}\n$$\n\nexists for every real $s>a,$ and $F$ is infinitely differentiable in this region of convergence. \n\nThe smoothness property states that, for each integer $n\\ge 0$ and $s>a,$ we have\n\n$$\n{F}^{(n)}(s)=(-1)^{n}\\,L{{t}^{n}f(t)}.\n$$\n\nLet's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Smoothness has no bearing on whether the Laplace transform vanishes.\nA function of exponential order always has a well-defined Laplace transform for $s>a$, and there is no reason for that transform to be identically zero.\n\n- Statement II is true. The smoothness theorem states that for $f(t)$ of exponential order, the Laplace transform\n\n$$\nF(s)=L{f}(s)\n$$\n\nis infinitely differentiable at every point in its region of convergence, and we have\n\n$$\n{F}^{(n)}(s)=(-1)^{n}\\,L{{t}^{n}f(t)}(s).\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. The Laplace transform $F(s)$ of a function $f(t)$ is always infinitely differentiable in its region of convergence, even if $f(t)$ is non-smooth.\n\nTherefore, the answer is \"II and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-332674/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "32e63c33-8820-542f-afab-f27a1f6a847a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-332674"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186220615 :answer-field/correct 17592186220616 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186220611 :answer-field/correct 17592186220613 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186220620 :answer-field/correct 17592186220623 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-334874"] :question/problem "Suppose that $f(t)$ is piecewise continuous on $[0,\\infty )$ and its Laplace transform\n\n$$\nF(s)=L{f(t)}\n$$\n\nexists for $s>a.$ Then, $F(s)$ is twice differentiable at every point $s>a,$ and we have\n\n$$\n{F}^{″}(s)=L{{t}^{2}\\cdot f(t)}.\n$$\n\nA proof of this statement is given below. \n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ $F(s)={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}f(t)\\,dt$ exists for $s>a.$\n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ ${F}^{″}(s)=\\frac{{d}^{2}}{d{s}^{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}f(t)\\,dt$\n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ ${F}^{″}(s)={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{{∂}^{2}}{∂{s}^{2}}({e}^{-st}f(t))\\,dt$\n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ $\\frac{{∂}^{2}}{∂{s}^{2}}({e}^{-st}f(t))={t}^{2}{e}^{-st}f(t)$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ ${F}^{″}(s)={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{t}^{2}{e}^{-st}f(t)\\,dt$\n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ ${F}^{″}(s)=L{{t}^{2}\\cdot f(t)}$\n\nSelect the correct options in the following reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L2}$ follows from line $\\text{L1}$ and\n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L3}$ follows from $\\text{L2}$ and {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L4}$ follows from {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "If a function $f(t)$ is piecewise continuous on $[0,\\infty )$ and has exponential order $a,$ then its Laplace transform\n\n$$\nF(s)=L{f(t)}\n$$\n\nexists for every real $s>a,$ and $F$ is infinitely differentiable in this region of convergence. \n\nThe smoothness property states that, for each integer $n\\ge 0$ and $s>a,$ we have\n\n$$\n{F}^{(n)}(s)=(-1)^{n}\\,L{{t}^{n}f(t)}.\n$$\n\nWe're asked to prove the smoothness property in the case $n=2.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- We first consider line $\\text{L2}.$ From line $\\text{L1}$ we know that\n\n$$\nF(s)={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}f(t)\\,dt.\n$$\n\nBy $\\text{the definition of the second derivative with respect to }s$, we get\n\n$$\n{F}^{″}(s)=\\frac{{d}^{2}}{d{s}^{2}}F(s)=\\frac{{d}^{2}}{d{s}^{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}f(t)\\,dt,\n$$\n\nwhich is exactly the statement in line $\\text{L2}.$\n\n- Next we consider line $\\text{L3}.$ From $\\text{L2}$ we have\n\n$$\n{F}^{″}(s)=\\frac{{d}^{2}}{d{s}^{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}f(t)\\,dt.\n$$\n\nSince $f$ is of exponential order, the integral converges, and we can\ndifferentiate under the integral sign:\n\n$$\n{F}^{″}(s)={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{{∂}^{2}}{∂{s}^{2}}({e}^{-st}f(t))\\,dt.\n$$\n\nTherefore, line $\\text{L3}$ follows from $\\text{L2}$ and $\\text{differentiating under the integral sign}.$\n\n- We now consider line $\\text{L4}.$ The function $f(t)$ does not depend on $s$, so\n\n$$\n\\frac{{∂}^{2}}{∂{s}^{2}}({e}^{-st}f(t))=f(t)\\,\\frac{{∂}^{2}}{∂{s}^{2}}({e}^{-st})=f(t)\\,\\frac{∂}{∂s}(-t{e}^{-st})=f(t)\\,({t}^{2}{e}^{-st})={t}^{2}{e}^{-st}f(t).\n$$\n\nThus line $\\text{L4}$ follows from $\\text{the chain rule}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186220717 :answer-field/correct 17592186220722 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-340844/field-2/d6fe4af71efbeaee817ab810557781588ef27cc120f4e4bcaade0285ef40d9f6" :answer/id #uuid "a469c26d-cf9c-55ab-a32f-2a9f2f2ce17a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{(s-4)^{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340844/field-2/d84a38bb3540f94335b6126e7d6146d24d0ef40b06b94c7ea2aef1869a2e9e69" :answer/id #uuid "18cc850c-90e9-59d3-a2bd-2e37ad1045b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{6}{(s-4)^{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340844/field-2/035cc8eaac5db197314a18b09344d1267f466921c9cee885a517fd5ef23c5aa9" :answer/id #uuid "15793f75-6f65-5df9-ba30-67d5f7d92711" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2s}{(s-4)^{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340844/field-2/c8a872a26b92101b983e78b23ed8f229e2dc3112b0663a2b8ea026d724d9f8bc" :answer/id #uuid "5b955eef-7455-54f9-a851-8c764b5d814a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{(s-4)^{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340844/field-2/64230fce96e60c9576cff508676641b269a898394ededc5b59bf93880f29da75" :answer/id #uuid "42052ce3-ea4e-531d-8291-b2609d0ac921" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{6}{(s-4)^{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340844/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "992b8799-4f9a-5ab7-b2d4-a9f80d62a058" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-340844/field-2/d6fe4af71efbeaee817ab810557781588ef27cc120f4e4bcaade0285ef40d9f6" :answer-field/choices ["q-340844/field-2/d6fe4af71efbeaee817ab810557781588ef27cc120f4e4bcaade0285ef40d9f6" "q-340844/field-2/d84a38bb3540f94335b6126e7d6146d24d0ef40b06b94c7ea2aef1869a2e9e69" "q-340844/field-2/035cc8eaac5db197314a18b09344d1267f466921c9cee885a517fd5ef23c5aa9" "q-340844/field-2/c8a872a26b92101b983e78b23ed8f229e2dc3112b0663a2b8ea026d724d9f8bc" "q-340844/field-2/64230fce96e60c9576cff508676641b269a898394ededc5b59bf93880f29da75"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-340844/field-3/d6fe4af71efbeaee817ab810557781588ef27cc120f4e4bcaade0285ef40d9f6" :answer/id #uuid "4952224e-25ba-55a8-a225-5c07a5746a03" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{(s-4)^{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340844/field-3/d995e9125c37cd363cd9b6bc03c7e1b02c3d221571332f2bfe3a0d67088a01b4" :answer/id #uuid "cf9294d4-5887-5ecc-9130-fc50fdf6e7d1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2s}{(s-4)^{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340844/field-3/c8a872a26b92101b983e78b23ed8f229e2dc3112b0663a2b8ea026d724d9f8bc" :answer/id #uuid "9b6c7c64-6929-556d-9d5d-c5c5f964c51c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{(s-4)^{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340844/field-3/035cc8eaac5db197314a18b09344d1267f466921c9cee885a517fd5ef23c5aa9" :answer/id #uuid "664eb1b8-b64e-5200-a18b-4c1d56773185" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2s}{(s-4)^{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340844/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "21f3ad76-b579-5693-bc4e-57d3a5110069" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-340844/field-3/d6fe4af71efbeaee817ab810557781588ef27cc120f4e4bcaade0285ef40d9f6" :answer-field/choices ["q-340844/field-3/d6fe4af71efbeaee817ab810557781588ef27cc120f4e4bcaade0285ef40d9f6" "q-340844/field-3/d995e9125c37cd363cd9b6bc03c7e1b02c3d221571332f2bfe3a0d67088a01b4" "q-340844/field-3/c8a872a26b92101b983e78b23ed8f229e2dc3112b0663a2b8ea026d724d9f8bc" "q-340844/field-3/035cc8eaac5db197314a18b09344d1267f466921c9cee885a517fd5ef23c5aa9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-340844"] :question/problem "Suppose we wish to calculate the Laplace transform $L{{t}^{2}{e}^{4t}}$ using the smoothness property. Select the correct options in the reasoning below.Let $f(t)={e}^{4t}$ and $F(s)=L{f(t)}.$ By the smoothness property of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\nL{{t}^{2}f(t)}={{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nWe have that\n\n$$\n{F}^{″}(s)={{field-2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nL{{t}^{2}{e}^{4t}}={{field-3}},\\,s>4.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If a function $f(t)$ is piecewise continuous on $[0,\\infty )$ and has exponential order $a,$ then its Laplace transform\n\n$$\nF(s)=L{f(t)}\n$$\n\nexists for every real $s>a,$ and $F$ is infinitely differentiable in this region of convergence. Moreover, for each integer $n\\ge 0$ and every such $s,$ we have\n\n$$\nL{{t}^{n}f(t)}=(-1)^{n}{F}^{(n)}(s).\n$$\n\nIn particular, for $n=2,$ we have\n\n$$\nL{{t}^{2}f(t)}={F}^{″}(s).\n$$\n\nWe have that $f(t)={e}^{4t}.$ Therefore, for $s>4,$ we have\n\n$$\nF(s)=\\frac{1}{s-4}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating with respect to $s,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}^{′}(s) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{1}{s-4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}((s-4)^{-1}) \\\\  & =-(s-4)^{-2} \\\\ {F}^{″}(s) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-(s-4)^{-2}) \\\\  & =2(s-4)^{-3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{(s-4)^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by the smoothness property,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{t}^{2}{e}^{4t}}={F}^{″}(s)=\\frac{2}{(s-4)^{3}},\\,s>4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-340844/field-2" "q-340844/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186220729 :answer-field/correct 17592186220732 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-340850/field-2/35325f03800b09b022e3c511bb543bd4c2424b496dbca1d644db68537d620b36" :answer/id #uuid "ac66a03a-359a-5e37-a080-93c185cd8aee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}+4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340850/field-2/913550794c96ea4103707acb9bc43474c4587fa864f84ba94baa0799dbd7f034" :answer/id #uuid "81da3657-863d-5f66-94c2-dfaa96b83067" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{{s}^{2}+4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340850/field-2/11dd6481f0e40af4774ec8fd8834114c9131bc8902b1a3c28b6485cdd880840a" :answer/id #uuid "47b590fc-5f86-52c6-bd92-5bc4f2b98b64" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{{s}^{2}+16}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340850/field-2/fc3e01b8052e2ebce262096a93fea386ec246d1818b86e9d2bfafe8b603d7af8" :answer/id #uuid "16f270b0-e92d-5c1f-aaeb-7028cf5a1c80" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}+16}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340850/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "0ad00210-691c-56eb-a6cd-4f290495347e" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-340850/field-2/11dd6481f0e40af4774ec8fd8834114c9131bc8902b1a3c28b6485cdd880840a" :answer-field/choices ["q-340850/field-2/35325f03800b09b022e3c511bb543bd4c2424b496dbca1d644db68537d620b36" "q-340850/field-2/913550794c96ea4103707acb9bc43474c4587fa864f84ba94baa0799dbd7f034" "q-340850/field-2/11dd6481f0e40af4774ec8fd8834114c9131bc8902b1a3c28b6485cdd880840a" "q-340850/field-2/fc3e01b8052e2ebce262096a93fea386ec246d1818b86e9d2bfafe8b603d7af8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-340850/field-3/f6cdaf8343f8c6f472b4a1e254c613936592593fcb27b64936f35a4d2bffce59" :answer/id #uuid "d00bcdc4-6d4d-5af0-ab30-3b96d9e44cb8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{24{s}^{2}-128}{({s}^{2}+16)^{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340850/field-3/374535a2b8719629b9d2f9a29a04bd501add2810962f1fa46b6169820044bf9b" :answer/id #uuid "e4c0f9c8-68be-5dd2-b8e8-53472b722ea9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{24{s}^{2}-32}{({s}^{2}+16)^{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340850/field-3/d640b987ccb3555ee81fd4a0bafa99d5e1a1ec86ed29c9968917f50276df1671" :answer/id #uuid "3cd2d340-8520-563c-9330-692982d27fde" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{16{s}^{2}-24}{({s}^{2}+16)^{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340850/field-3/a714ed3808237f477c0497180bc54b79141b57f2cd75b10ef1ac9db7f5b2f6f4" :answer/id #uuid "080854da-e2f9-527e-84b6-8c8c531b3db2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{16{s}^{2}-128}{({s}^{2}+16)^{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340850/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "5127ddb6-0fa1-5832-9797-d20722f77f41" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-340850/field-3/f6cdaf8343f8c6f472b4a1e254c613936592593fcb27b64936f35a4d2bffce59" :answer-field/choices ["q-340850/field-3/f6cdaf8343f8c6f472b4a1e254c613936592593fcb27b64936f35a4d2bffce59" "q-340850/field-3/374535a2b8719629b9d2f9a29a04bd501add2810962f1fa46b6169820044bf9b" "q-340850/field-3/d640b987ccb3555ee81fd4a0bafa99d5e1a1ec86ed29c9968917f50276df1671" "q-340850/field-3/a714ed3808237f477c0497180bc54b79141b57f2cd75b10ef1ac9db7f5b2f6f4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-340850/field-4/f6cdaf8343f8c6f472b4a1e254c613936592593fcb27b64936f35a4d2bffce59" :answer/id #uuid "cd199073-2260-55d6-b52c-cf38cb326d40" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{24{s}^{2}-128}{({s}^{2}+16)^{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340850/field-4/f1183c1c740bd2cff4518c99ba76c3e7a4d93c5ad60a753c007e3487b2fbfdea" :answer/id #uuid "d537406d-c3ee-5d4b-bd54-2fc366d3a96a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{24{s}^{3}-128s}{({s}^{2}+16)^{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340850/field-4/28042a476b7b801301f8fe614e6271282ad53b9899c29a1477cfff8dda010e52" :answer/id #uuid "140cc551-bcdf-5485-bb12-a67ff7d370ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{24{s}^{3}-128s}{({s}^{2}+16)^{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340850/field-4/2f4228599e9c8508ab5ee7fd4713ef54aced41ddd2f0e23da644e0c4aeceb8ca" :answer/id #uuid "2582560d-da54-5dea-a97c-a3041dc0419a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{24{s}^{2}-128}{({s}^{2}+16)^{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340850/field-4" :answer-field/id #uuid "f7fbdc18-5153-522f-8eec-415d5c6ad820" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-340850/field-4/f6cdaf8343f8c6f472b4a1e254c613936592593fcb27b64936f35a4d2bffce59" :answer-field/choices ["q-340850/field-4/f6cdaf8343f8c6f472b4a1e254c613936592593fcb27b64936f35a4d2bffce59" "q-340850/field-4/f1183c1c740bd2cff4518c99ba76c3e7a4d93c5ad60a753c007e3487b2fbfdea" "q-340850/field-4/28042a476b7b801301f8fe614e6271282ad53b9899c29a1477cfff8dda010e52" "q-340850/field-4/2f4228599e9c8508ab5ee7fd4713ef54aced41ddd2f0e23da644e0c4aeceb8ca"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-340850"] :question/problem "Suppose we wish to calculate the Laplace transform \n\n$$\nL{{t}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t}.\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below. You may make use of the following result:\n\n$$\nL{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t}=\\frac{\\omega }{{s}^{2}+{\\omega }^{2}},\\,s>0.\n$$\n\nLet $f(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t$ and $F(s)=L{f(t)}.$ By the smoothness property of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\nL{{t}^{2}f(t)}={{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nThe Laplace transform of $f(t)$ is\n\n$$\nF(s)=L{f(t)}={{field-2}},\\,s>0.\n$$\n\nWe have that\n\n$$\n{F}^{″}(s)={{field-3}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nL{{t}^{2}{e}^{4t}}={{field-4}},\\,s>0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If a function $f(t)$ is piecewise continuous on $[0,\\infty )$ and has exponential order $a,$ then its Laplace transform\n\n$$\nF(s)=L{f(t)}\n$$\n\nexists for every real $s>a,$ and $F$ is infinitely differentiable in this region of convergence. Moreover, for each integer $n\\ge 0$ and every such $s,$ we have\n\n$$\nL{{t}^{n}f(t)}=(-1)^{n}{F}^{(n)}(s).\n$$\n\nIn particular, for $n=2,$ we have\n\n$$\nL{{t}^{2}f(t)}={F}^{″}(s).\n$$\n\nWe have that $f(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t.$ Using the given result with $\\omega =4,$ the Laplace transform of $f(t)$ is \n\n$$\nF(s)=\\frac{4}{{s}^{2}+16},\\,s>0.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating with respect to $s,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}^{′}(s) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{4}{{s}^{2}+16}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(4({s}^{2}+16)^{-1}) \\\\  & =-4({s}^{2}+16)^{-2}\\cdot 2s \\\\  & =-\\frac{8s}{({s}^{2}+16)^{2}} \\\\ {F}^{″}(s) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-\\frac{8s}{({s}^{2}+16)^{2}}) \\\\  & =-8\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{s}{({s}^{2}+16)^{2}}) \\\\  & =-8\\cdot (\\frac{(s)^{′}\\cdot ({s}^{2}+16)^{2}-s\\cdot {(({s}^{2}+16)^{2})}^{′}}{({s}^{2}+16)^{4}}) \\\\  & =-8\\cdot (\\frac{({s}^{2}+16)^{2}-s\\cdot 2({s}^{2}+16)\\cdot 2s}{({s}^{2}+16)^{4}}) \\\\  & =-8\\cdot (\\frac{({s}^{2}+16)^{2}-4{s}^{2}({s}^{2}+16)}{({s}^{2}+16)^{4}}) \\\\  & =-8\\cdot (\\frac{{s}^{2}+16-4{s}^{2}}{({s}^{2}+16)^{3}}) \\\\  & =-8\\cdot (\\frac{16-3{s}^{2}}{({s}^{2}+16)^{3}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{24{s}^{2}-128}{({s}^{2}+16)^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we used the quotient rule to find ${F}^{″}(s).$\n\nTherefore, by the smoothness property,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{t}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t}={F}^{″}(s)=\\frac{24{s}^{2}-128}{({s}^{2}+16)^{3}},\\,s>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-340850/field-2" "q-340850/field-3" "q-340850/field-4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
